<title>TAIWAN: Bank of Taiwan sets slight interest-rate cuts.</title>
<headline>Bank of Taiwan sets slight interest-rate cuts.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-owned Bank of Taiwan, the island's leading commercial bank, said on Wednesday it would cut interest rates for its one-to-three-year time deposits by 0.05-0.20 percentage points, effective from Thursday.</p>
<p>The reduction was to reflect the market's current interest rate level, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
